    "result_text": "All green. The build succeeds and the acceptance test passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a derived `riskFlag` to the owner response that is true when any of the three risk signals hold, else false.\n\n**Where each piece went:**\n\n1. **`util/DisposableEmailDomains.java`** (new) \u2014 single home for disposable-email-provider knowledge. Holds the one blocklist and derives everything from it: `domainOf(email)`, `isBlocked(domain)` (exact blocklist match), and `isDisposableAdjacent(domain)` (belongs to a known provider family \u2014 a subdomain like `x.mailinator.com` or an alternate suffix like `mailinator.net` \u2014 detected via the providers' second-level labels, computed from the blocklist so nothing is duplicated).\n\n2. **`ValidateEmailDomain.java`** \u2014 refactored to reuse `DisposableEmailDomains.domainOf(...)` + `isBlocked(...)` instead of its own private copy of the domain set and parsing. Behaviour unchanged (outright-blocked domains still 400).\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.riskFlag(owner)`** \u2014 a small derived-field method (sitting alongside the other `@Mapping` expression derivations) that ORs the three conditions: `possibleDuplicate` (stored), `capacityWarning` (stored \u2014 \"over soft capacity\"), and `isDisposableAdjacent` of the stored email's domain. Null-safe on the two `Boolean` flags.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `riskFlag` boolean to the `Owner` schema so the generated DTO exposes it; the mapper populates it and both the GET and create responders return it via the existing `toOwnerDto`.\n\nThe flag is computed purely from the stored owner at read time, so it's consistent across GET/POST/PUT without adding a new persisted column or a new pipeline step, and the disposable-domain logic lives in exactly one place.",
